    "https://emploi.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/working-at-uga/uga-in-numbers/": {
      "title": "UGA in numbers",
      "description": "UGA in numbers - Emploi - Université Grenoble Alpes Université Grenoble Alpes Practical informations Contacts Campuses map English FR - Français EN - English Job site Welcome Search Open the main menu Open the search engine EN Close the mobile menu Working at UGA Careers Job Offers Competitive Exams Practical informations Université Grenoble Alpes Close the mobile menu Return UGA in numbers Recruitment process View the entire section Close the mobile menu Return Senior Lecturers and Professors Fixed-term Contract Faculty Members PhD Students and Researchers View the entire section Close the mobile menu Return Temporary Teaching and Research Assistants (ATER) Lecturers and Lecturer-researchers Lecteurs and Maîtres de Langues (Native Speaker Assistants) View the entire section Close the mobile menu Return Contacts Campuses map View the entire section Close the mobile menu FR - Français EN - English Working at UGA Careers Job Offers Competitive Exams LinkedIn Instagram You are here: Home Working at UGA UGA in numbers UGA in numbers UGA in numbers 57,000 students 10,500 employees Human resources 10,500 staff (including 2,550 from national research organisations). 6,050 teachers, lecturers and researchers (including 1,430 researchers from national research organisations and 1,000 contractual doctoral students). 4,450 administrative and technical staff (including 1,120 from national research organisations). International 11,000 international students 1 in 5 students is a foreigner 150 different nationalities 432% of PhD students are foreigners 30% Master's taught in English 19 languages taught 1 200 international university partnerships 1 special office providing personalized services for international students (ISSO) Research 69 research units 13 Labex and 7 Equipex 3,000 PhD students 137 ERC since 2007 : 51 ERC Starting Grants 32 ERC Consolidator Grants (started in 2013) 31 ERC Advanced Grants 18 ERC Proof of Concept 5 ERC Synergy Grant 32 CNRS medals since 2001: 1 gold medal 28 silver medals 3 innovation medals 160 members or honorary members of the Institut Universitaire de France (including 32 junior or senior members in delegation) Top 150 in Shanghai global ranking 2024 Shanghai thematic ranking 2023: Top 50 in 6 disciplines Top 100 in 15 disciplines Campus and student life 13 campuses spread over 6 departments (Isère, Drôme, Ardèche, Savoie, Haute-Savoie, Hautes-Alpes) 3 places of culture and creation: Amphidice, Espace scénique transdisciplinaire (EST), Maison de la création et de l'innovation (MACI) Libraries open 83 hours a week : evenings, Saturdays and Sundays 40 student life places 200 students association including an orchestra, dance group, 2 choirs and a student radio stations Over 130 cultural events on campuses each year 39 sports disciplines open to all 600 top-level student athletes and 150 top-level artists students 120 student-entrepreneurs 2,160 students with disabilities supported each year International rankings Université Grenoble Alpes ranks each year in the Top 100-250 group of the best world universities in all major international rankings, and is in the Top 10 of French higher education institutions. Find out more Print Share Share this on Facebook Share this on LinkedIn Working at UGA UGA in numbers Recruitment process Université Grenoble Alpes Direction générale déléguée aux Ressources humaines 1180 avenue Centrale 38400 Saint-Martin-d'Hères France +33 (0)4 57 42 21 42 Legal notices Personal data Credits Data protection policy Cookies Accessibility: not compliant Sitemap Follow us LinkedIn Instagram URL of the page https://emploi.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/working-at-uga/uga-in-numbers/uga-in-numbers-838859.kjsp?RH=1681204071167 Page title UGA in numbers - Emploi - Université Grenoble Alpes Share the link Copy Copied Close the modal window Share the URL of this page I recommend: Consultable at this address: La page sera alors accessible depuis votre menu \"Mes favoris\". Stop video 