    "https://emploi.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/data-protection-policy/": {
      "title": "Data protection policy",
      "description": "Data protection policy - Emploi - Université Grenoble Alpes Université Grenoble Alpes Practical informations Contacts Campuses map English FR - Français EN - English Job site Welcome Search Open the main menu Open the search engine EN Close the mobile menu Working at UGA Careers Job Offers Competitive Exams Practical informations Université Grenoble Alpes Close the mobile menu Return UGA in numbers Recruitment process View the entire section Close the mobile menu Return Senior Lecturers and Professors Fixed-term Contract Faculty Members PhD Students and Researchers View the entire section Close the mobile menu Return Temporary Teaching and Research Assistants (ATER) Lecturers and Lecturer-researchers Lecteurs and Maîtres de Langues (Native Speaker Assistants) View the entire section Close the mobile menu Return Contacts Campuses map View the entire section Close the mobile menu FR - Français EN - English Working at UGA Careers Job Offers Competitive Exams LinkedIn Instagram You are here: Home Data protection policy Data protection policy Information notice Data protection Identity of the data controller Université Grenoble Alpes Human Resources Department (DGD RH) Bâtiment Stendhal Purpose of the processing Purposes The UGA processes your personal data as part of its staff recruitment activities and for the following purposes Receipt of unsolicited or unsolicited applications (CVs, etc.); Management of the suitability of profiles for the position concerned and selection of relevant profiles; Qualification of applications and sharing with the institution's internal recruitment officers; Correspondence with candidates (progress of the process, hiring, rejection of the application, etc.); Reporting and statistics; Retention of applications within the legal time limits Legal basis for processing personal data The UGA processes your personal data on the basis of its legitimate interest for recruitment purposes. *Article 6-f of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) Data processed When you apply for a job, the UGA collects the following personal data: - Civil status data (title, name, contact details), - Professional data from your curriculum vitae - your salary, - Connection data Duration of data storage Your personal data is kept for the legal retention periods or for the period necessary for the purposes for which it was collected. According to the recommendations of the CNIL, in the event of an unsuccessful application, your file will be kept for 2 years from the date of receipt of the application. During this period, the UGA may contact you again in the event that your profile is suitable for a new job offer, if you have given your consent. * Deliberation n°02-017 of 21 March 2002 of the CNIL Recipients of the data Access to your personal data is strictly limited to the institution's internal recruiters, the DGHR, and the subcontractor in the context of the service provided by the Talentlink recruitment tool. Exercise of rights Under certain conditions, you may exercise the following rights regarding your personal data: Right of access ; Right of rectification; Right to erasure; Right to limitation of processing; Right to object. To exercise your rights or for any questions about the processing of your data, you can contact the DGDRH dgdrh-recrutement@univ-grenoble-alpes.fr or the UGA Data Protection Officer at the following address dpo@univ-grenoble-alpes.fr If, after contacting us, you feel that your rights have not been respected or that the present data processing does not comply with data protection rules, you have the right to lodge a complaint with the CNIL Print Share Share this on Facebook Share this on LinkedIn Published on  April 11, 2023 Updated on April 11, 2023 Data protection policy Université Grenoble Alpes Direction générale déléguée aux Ressources humaines 1180 avenue Centrale 38400 Saint-Martin-d'Hères France +33 (0)4 57 42 21 42 Legal notices Personal data Credits Data protection